## Summary

The instability was in `bedtools fisher`'s shared sorted-overlap sweep, `NewChromSweep`.

### Root cause

`bedtools fisher` (like `bedtools jaccard`) is built on `IntersectFile`, which uses `NewChromSweep` for sorted inputs. The sweep intentionally stops early once no further overlaps are possible:

```cpp
// NewChromsweep.cpp
if (allCurrDBrecsNull() && allCachesEmpty() && !_runToQueryEnd) {
    _testLastQueryRec = true;
    return false;
}
```

When that happens, `NewChromSweep::closeOut()` drains the *remaining query records* unconditionally, but only drains the *remaining database records* when its `testChromOrderVal` argument is `true`:

```cpp
void NewChromSweep::closeOut(bool testChromOrderVal) {
    ...
    while (!_queryFRM->eof()) { ... }          // query always drained
    if (testChromOrderVal) {                    // database only drained here
        for (int i = 0; i < _numDBs; i++) {
            while (!_dbFRMs[i]->eof()) { ... }
        }
    }
}
```

`Jaccard::finalizeCalculations()` calls `_sweep->closeOut(true)`, but the `Fisher` override called `_sweep->closeOut()` with the default `false`. So database intervals that could never overlap the query (e.g., on chromosomes after the last query chromosome) were never read into the sweep totals, and `Number of db intervals` stayed incomplete while the Fisher table used the incomplete marginal.

### Fix

`source/src/fisher/fisher.cpp`:

```diff
 bool Fisher::finalizeCalculations()
 {
-    _sweep->closeOut();
+    // Fisher reports a complete contingency table, so drain any remaining
+    // database records (not just the queries) to include them in the
+    // database marginal totals even when they cannot overlap the queries.
+    _sweep->closeOut(true);
     _queryUnion = _sweep->getQueryTotalRecordLength();
     ...
```

This is the same call the base `Jaccard` implementation already makes, and it is safe for Fisher because Fisher requires `-g` (a genome file), which makes the sweep's chrom-order check a no-op. Ordinary overlap commands (`intersect`, etc.) are untouched.

### Verification

- `python reproduce.py` now exits 0 with `public_reproduction_passed: true`; the augmented database reports 6 db intervals (up from 3), overlaps stay 2, the contingency table is consistent, and the p-values shift.
- `source/test/fisher/test-fisher.sh`: all 5 tests pass.
- `source/test/jaccard/test-jaccard.sh`: all 16 tests pass.
- `source/test/intersect/test-intersect.sh`: all 239 tests pass, confirming ordinary overlap behavior is preserved.

